# Adding a directory integration (auto-launch / “auto-pilot”)

**Agent:** Ship **one PR** that completes every item in [PR checklist](#pr-checklist). Directory launches are **not** social `SocialProvider` channels: users keep a **business profile** in OpenQuok, open the directory site in their browser, and the **OpenQuok extension** autofills forms from `extension_config` after a dashboard handoff. Also follow **backend-migrations-naming**, **backend-migrations-seed**, **source-project-neutrality**, and **company-brand-icons** for logos.

**Extended reference:** field mapping, step rail behavior, and manual smoke tests — `docs/auto-launch/extension-ui-patterns.md`.

**Contrast with social providers:** See **add-social-provider-integration.mdc** for OAuth/credentials/extension **posting** channels. Directory integrations reuse the **browser extension** install path (`BrowserExtensionConnectDialog`, `VITE_OPENQUOK_BROWSER_EXTENSION_ID`) but do **not** add `backend/integrations/providers/*` or composer preview tiles unless you are also shipping a social channel.

## Connect family (v1)

| Path | User flow | Backend | Extension |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Extension directory launch** (only shipped path) | My Products → Add directory launch / Launch → extension handoff → user submits on directory site | `auto_launch_destinations` + `submissions/intent` API | Per-`provider_slug` content script + shared fill engine |

`submission_path = 'auto'` is reserved; do not implement server-side submit in the same PR unless explicitly scoped.

## Identifier contract

| Concept | Format | Where it must match |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Site slug** | kebab-case, DNS-like (`peerpush`, `uneed`) | `link_directory_sites.slug`, Add Channel tile grouping (`directorySiteKeyFromProviderSlug`), bundled logo path `/icons/link-directory/{slug}.svg` |
| **Opportunity slug** | kebab-case per listing path (`standard-launch`, `free-queue`, `paid-launch`) | `link_directory_opportunities.slug` (unique per `site_id`) |
| **Provider slug** | `{site}-{variant}` or stable product name (`peerpush-standard-launch`, `uneed-join-line`) | `auto_launch_destinations.provider_slug`, `link_directory_opportunities.auto_launch_provider_slug`, `extension` content script registration, `common/src/browser-extension/pageAssist.ts` `directoryLaunchProviders`, handoff JWT / tests |

One **published** `auto_launch_destinations` row per executable variant. Multiple variants on one site can share `picker_group_key` / `picker_group_title` so Add Channel shows one card with a variant picker.

## Data model (two layers)

1. **Editorial / SEO (link directory)** — `link_directory_sites` + `link_directory_opportunities` (cost, dofollow, steps, CTA). Surfaces on **Build backlinks** hub and secret-admin link-directory manager.
2. **Executable (auto-launch)** — `auto_launch_destinations.extension_config` (steps, `profilePath`, `fillMode`, `proof`) + `start_url`. Surfaces on **Account → My Products**, Add Channel directory tiles, extension.

Wire opportunities to destinations:

- `link_directory_opportunities.auto_launch_enabled = true`
- `link_directory_opportunities.auto_launch_provider_slug = <provider_slug>`
- `auto_launch_destinations.link_directory_opportunity_id` → opportunity UUID

Opportunity metadata flows to the dashboard as `opportunityDofollow`, `opportunityCostNote`, etc. (`AutoLaunchRepository` join → `AutoLaunchDTO`).

### Dofollow / cost (catalog)

| `dofollow` | UI badge (directory launch picker) |
| --- | --- |
| `dofollow` | Dofollow |
| `nofollow` | Nofollow |
| `unknown` | Link type unknown |
| `null` | (hidden) |

Label helper: `web/src/lib/auto-launch/utils/directoryLaunchPickerLabels.ts`. Prefer **`dofollow`** for paid listing paths when the directory documents a normal website link; use **`unknown`** for free/conditional tiers when policy is unclear (mirror Uneed Join the line). Do not guess `nofollow` without editorial evidence.

## SQL seeds (typical new site)

Follow **backend-migrations-naming**: `link-directory/504_<YYYYMMDD>_seed_<subject>.sql`, `auto-launch/503_<YYYYMMDD>_seed_<subject>_destination.sql` (adjust numeric prefix within tier). Use real calendar date in filename and `MODULE DATE` header.

| Step | File / location | What to add |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | `backend/supabase/db/link-directory/504_*_seed_<site>.sql` | `link_directory_sites` row (slug, title, `site_url`, `logo_url`, metrics, tags) |
| 2 | Same file | One or more `link_directory_opportunities` rows (`dofollow`, `cost_tier`, `cost_note`, `description`, `steps`, `cta_href`, `auto_launch_*`) |
| 3 | `backend/supabase/db/auto-launch/503_*_seed_<site>_destination.sql` | `INSERT INTO auto_launch_destinations` with full `extension_config` JSON (`version`, `startUrlPatterns`, `readyUrlHint`, `steps[]`, `proof`) |
| 4 | — | Re-run `node backend/scripts/aggregate_migrations_all.mjs` (never edit aggregated `supabase/migrations/*_core_structure.sql` by hand) |

**Reference seeds:** Uneed — `link-directory/502_20251001_seed_link_directory_exemplar.sql` + `auto-launch/502_20261013_seed_uneed_destinations.sql`. PeerPush — `link-directory/504_20261016_seed_peerpush.sql` + `auto-launch/503_20261016_seed_peerpush_destination.sql`.

**Storage:** Profile logo/gallery uploads use bucket seeded in `auto-launch/502_20261013_seed_uneed_destinations.sql` (`auto_launch_profile_media`).

## `extension_config` authoring

| Field | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `startUrlPatterns` | Host/path globs where the content script may run |
| `readyUrlHint` | Substring hint for “on the right page” (e.g. `pricing`, `submit`) |
| `steps[].fields[]` | `profilePath` (e.g. `name`, `profile_data.categories`), `fillMode` (`text`, `rich_html`, `tags`, `select`, `boolean`, file) |
| `proof` | `successPathRegex`, `listingUrlSelector` for completion / listing URL capture |

Readiness and card hints use the same paths (`common/src/auto-launch/profileLaunchReadiness.ts`). When adding fields, update:

- `web/src/lib/ui/components/auto-launch/ProductProfileComposer.svelte` (if users must edit them)
- `web/src/lib/auto-launch/businessProfileFormValidation.ts` (which composer tab opens on error)
- `common/src/auto-launch/businessProfileData.ts` limits if new arrays/tags apply

Extension fill behavior: `extension/src/directory-launch/fillEngine.ts`, `profileValues.ts` (+ `fillEngine.test.ts` for tag/array quirks).

## Browser extension

| Step | File |
| --- | --- |
| Register provider metadata | `common/src/browser-extension/pageAssist.ts` — add to `directoryLaunchProviders` (identifier, name, `contentScriptEntry`, `hostPatterns`, `hostPermission`) |
| Content script entry | `extension/src/content/directory-launch/<provider-slug>.ts` — `registerDirectoryLaunchProvider('<provider-slug>')` |
| Build | `extension/scripts/build-extension.mjs` — `contentScriptSpecs` row |
| Manifest | `extension/manifest.json` — `content_scripts` block (`matches` + `js` path) |
| Rebuild | `pnpm common:build` then `pnpm --filter @openquok/browser-extension build`; reload unpacked `extension/dist` |

`getDirectoryLaunchProvider(providerSlug)` must resolve or the content script logs a warning and no-ops.

## Backend API (usually unchanged per destination)

Routes: `backend/routes/AutoLaunchRoute.ts`. Service/repository: `backend/services/AutoLaunchService.ts`, `backend/repositories/AutoLaunchRepository.ts`. DTOs: `backend/utils/dtos/AutoLaunchDTO.ts`.

Add or extend **unit tests** in `backend/services/AutoLaunchService.unit.test.ts` when behavior changes (intent token, submission lifecycle). Launch tokens: `backend/utils/auth/launchToken.unit.test.ts`.

